{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact head a5ac712262cef0aadde2b5e845b3a8f18c73dd75, Lane C's own delta from 845c7fd7. All 31 named artifacts reviewed. The inherited contract is separately under review; this verdict identifies policy-runtime repairs, not another custody finding.\n\nValidation: npm ci --ignore-scripts, strict workspace typecheck, all 138 supplied tests under Node, and the same 138 tests under workerd pass. Compared the evaluator with atseq's actual source and reviewed the ported corpus, fingerprints and helper/activation/carry tests. Five independent reproductions in checker-owned /tmp/artroom-checker-policy/packages/policy/test/checker-review.test.ts show the observations below on BOTH Node and workerd. No live deployment or production mutation was performed. The extra tests assert observed buggy behavior for reproducibility; they are not claimed as product acceptance tests.\n\nP1.1 Record every input that determines a decision, including aggregate budget context (rules.ts ask/retain/evaluation/evaluateNotify; evaluator.ts ActMeter; explain.ts; profile.ts).\n- Using the DEFAULT act budget and a valid policy with a refuse scan followed by a require scan over 60 ordinary paths: refuse passes using 130 steps / 2,815,716 inspected bytes. Require then records policy-budget-exceeded (97 steps / 1,389,007 bytes). Replaying that require's retained input under the same policy and stamp, as the README and R-EVAL-6 prescribe, instead creates obl_scan-require (130 steps / 2,807,074 bytes). Both decisions have input digest sha256:8b321d7ddc7ae7e128649a0aacb514c93794cb46b41deb61d5407d9f8e3d7530. Earlier usage and limits are hidden mutable inputs.\n- An unconditional notify to role:admin yields @alice with directory A and @bob with directory B, with identical retained input digest sha256:d6ce06188a31491f8858e5c882cc45ca1602656b91c45ad6c77955963f34424f, policy, stamp and usage. NotifyDirectory is not retained.\nThe package's public explain data cannot replay these recorded outcomes from the advertised retained inputs. Retain and digest a complete replay context (budget limits and starting usage, and the notification directory; any other outcome-determining side inputs), or provide and retain an explicit ordered whole-act replay record with a defined reconstruction path. Version the aggregate budget/accounting as part of the protocol/profile and align it with the contract, rather than leaving ACT_BUDGET an undocumented behavioral parameter behind the same stamp. Keep aggregate safeguards; removing them is not the requested fix. Add both default-budget cross-kind replay and notify role/reviewer-directory replay cases on both hosts. Clarify the separate post-commit notify budget/retry context so a queue retry cannot inherit an accidental meter.\n\nP1.2 Return an owned immutable retained snapshot, and hash/evaluate that same snapshot (rules.ts retain and RuleEvaluation.input).\nretain assigns json = input and returns that original object; only PreparedInput is copied/frozen. After a successful evaluateRefuse, its RuleEvaluation.input === the caller input. Changing the caller's room field changes the returned retained input digest from sha256:5ac0970fc715daee3b516389b16110c8cc4e0aa573354fa993b80cc948e165ce to sha256:b7051b00035b2c471a168961f65fe81436db986c11bf8e944c8de90a3275c287 while Decision.input stays the first digest. Mutating during an await can likewise separate hashed and evaluated content. Own and freeze the complete snapshot before asynchronous hashing/evaluation; use the same owned content for the digest, PreparedInput and returned retention data. Preserve deterministic oversized-input refusals and the profile's bounds. Regress caller mutation both after return and while hashing/evaluation is pending.\n\nP1.3 Separate historical evidence authority from current initiator authority (admin.ts AdminApprovalFacts and judgeAdminApproval).\nThe facts explicitly say role is the reviewer's role NOW at reservation, and the function rejects it if not admin. A non-author who approved as an admin and was subsequently demoted under the default retirement policy is rejected with counts:false, admin-required, reopens:true, although R-REV-1 says role change/removal/default retirement/expired delegation do not reopen admitted evidence. Conversely the API cannot distinguish a promoted current admin from someone who was an admin at the review's admission.\nUse the recorded admission authority when deciding whether the review qualified for obl_admin-approval, plus current evidence validity under R-REV (including compromise of signer or grantor). Check the land initiator's current admin authority separately. Preserve the explicit current sole-admin count check for FLAGGED self-approval, rather than applying current reviewer membership/role to all earlier approvals. Add an ordinary non-self admin approval followed by demotion/removal/retirement that still counts, a member's old review followed by promotion that cannot become an admin approval, and the compromised/second-admin reopening cases.\n\nP2.1 Encode arbitrary legal repository paths safely in rule inputs (rules.ts ownersFor, policy.ts PolicyProposal.owners and values.ts reserved keys).\nRoot files constructor, prototype and _jsonata_cache are valid paths and glob literals, but ownersFor emits them as reserved JSON object keys; evaluateRequire then throws retryable policy-runtime instead of evaluating. __proto__ also changes the map's prototype because ownersFor uses {} assignment, producing 'expected plain object'. This is reproducible with an ordinary require-all rule and the actual fixture builder, not malicious evaluator bindings. Use an input representation that preserves arbitrary paths without reserved-key/prototype hazards, for example path/principal pairs, with an explicit contract change or a specified reversible safe encoding. Null-prototype maps alone do not solve the evaluator's reserved-key rejection. Do not broaden the restricted engine's profile silently or exclude otherwise legal Git paths to work around it. Add ownership, require, notify and replay cases for these paths on both hosts.\n\nArchitecture: the pure evaluator/rule/activation boundaries and Node/workerd parity are promising. Fresh per-call JSONata instances eliminate the spike's shared-hook race; unexpected engine faults propagate, and failed require rules refuse instead of dropping obligations. However the replay data model still omits determining state, and admin evidence uses the wrong time boundary. These must be correct before the Room depends on this package.\nSecurity: changes requested for immutable, complete decision inputs and historical authority. The path-key collision also includes prototype mutation at ownersFor. No signing keys or repository write credentials enter this runtime.\nSimplification: use one immutable replay context and one explicit recorded-authority model; keep host side inputs out of ad hoc optional mutable arguments unless they are included in that context. A safe path data shape is clearer than a growing set of filename exceptions.\n\nDocumentation limits: the profile.ts claim that 25,000 steps is 'at most about 225 ms of CPU' is stronger than the spike supports. Measurements gave an estimated 3-9 microseconds per step on sampled rules, not a worst-case CPU bound across admitted programs or hosts; describe it as an estimate. The 35 mutation spot-checks were reported by builder and were not independently rerun; the read source, independent reproductions, supplied suite and cross-host outputs are the review evidence here. Other listed contract gaps can remain explicit handoff work where they do not break these invariants. Full functional scope is preserved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e39d5c04cc581954d02bfa09fa8a1b0491c99af3","binding":"assigned","head":"a5ac712262cef0aadde2b5e845b3a8f18c73dd75","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fea17cabcdc24c47ba7ae69f7ec9779f2bc9f339\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f182d666b11580e68fef19ba9f458008c95b5845\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3226f55514fa803cc2d0e8ca3411c5575f32c756","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}